stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING
    PENDING --> SUCCEEDED: worker delivers
    PENDING --> RETRY_WAIT: retryable failure, attempts remain
    PENDING --> DLQ: non-retryable failure, or attempts exhausted

    RETRY_WAIT --> QUEUED: due retry + outbox committed atomically
    QUEUED --> SUCCEEDED: worker delivers
    QUEUED --> RETRY_WAIT: retryable failure, attempts remain
    QUEUED --> DLQ: non-retryable failure, or attempts exhausted

    DLQ --> RETRY_WAIT: manual replay (attempt_count reset to 0)

    note right of PENDING
        No separate DELIVERING state: a worker's
        ownership lives in an expiring PostgreSQL
        UUID lease. Redis pending messages are
        transport hints - see DECISIONS.md #31.
    end note
